# Runpod watchdog

GPU pods bill until stop/terminate. After any Runpod create or reuse:

1. Poll container logs on a short loop (2–3 min). Do not wait for the user.
2. Terminate the pod on `CAMPAIGN_DONE`, `CAMPAIGN_FAIL`, a crash loop (same traceback repeating), GPU idle through a failed assemble/eq, or the campaign wall (`MAX_GPU_HOURS`, currently 4 h).
3. Do not `sleep` the container to preserve logs. That keeps the meter running.
4. Do not recreate a pod to fix a crash loop if the same machine can be patched. Stop the loop, then run the job.
5. NMR ensembles are not campaign structures. Use an X-ray (or EM) PDB; one biological copy only.

`scripts/runpod_watchdog.py --kill` self-deletes when `RUNPOD_API_KEY` is in the pod env. If that print is `WATCHDOG_CANNOT_KILL`, terminate from this session via `pod-action terminate` / `delete-pod`.
